@page "/today"
@using PullbackStrategyLab.Web.Shell
@model TodayModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Today";
    SetupsView chosen = Model.Chosen;
    ExperimentView e = Model.Experiment;
}
@*
    What the lab is watching, from 7.20, for a reader who wants the answer rather than the workings.

    The two sides are two blocks with their own headings and no combined count, on the same terms
    the gallery draws them.
    see: Long and short are never pooled into one figure
*@
<h1>What the lab is watching</h1>

@if (chosen.Nothing is not null)
{
    <div class="empty-state">
        <p>Nothing to show: @chosen.Nothing.</p>
    </div>
}
else
{
    <p class="lede">Chosen on the evening of <b>@chosen.AsOf</b> out of @Model.Recorded.ToString("N0")
       names the lab recorded that evening, and live from the next session the market opens. The lab
       keeps no holiday calendar, so it names the evening that chose the list rather than guessing
       the date it trades on.</p>

    @if (e.Risk is ExperimentRiskView risk)
    {
        <p class="lede">Each one risks at most <b>@risk.Budget.ToString("C0")</b> of imaginary money,
           which is @risk.FractionInWords of the lab's @risk.Equity.ToString("C0").</p>
    }

    <div class="caveat">
        <b>No prices here, and that is deliberate.</b> The lab does not decide what to pay the
        evening before. Each plan carries a rule, and the price, the stop and the number of shares
        are all worked out at the minute the stock actually triggers. Writing a price tonight would
        be pretending to know something it cannot know until tomorrow.
    </div>

    @foreach (var side in new[]
    {
        (Name: "Stocks it would buy", Cards: chosen.Long, Css: "long"),
        (Name: "Stocks it would sell short", Cards: chosen.Short, Css: "short"),
    })
    {
        <section class="side">
            <h2>@side.Name</h2>

            @if (side.Cards.Count == 0)
            {
                <p class="muted">None this evening. A side that chooses nobody is an ordinary
                   outcome of the checks rather than a fault.</p>
            }
            else
            {
                <table class="chosen">
                    <caption>@side.Cards.Count name@(side.Cards.Count == 1 ? "" : "s"), ranked as the lab ranked them. This
                             count is for this side only and is never added to the other.</caption>
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th scope="col">Stock</th>
                            <th scope="col">Waiting for</th>
                            <th scope="col">Checks it passed</th>
                            <th scope="col">Noted against it</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        @foreach (SetupCardView card in side.Cards)
                        {
                            <tr>
                                <td class="tk @side.Css">@card.Ticker</td>
                                <td>a dip to its level, then a recovery</td>
                                <td class="num">@card.Checks.Count(c => c.Passed) of @card.Checks.Count</td>
                                <td>
                                    @{
                                        var noted = Model.PassedOnATechnicality(card);
                                    }
                                    @if (noted.Count == 0)
                                    {
                                        <span class="muted">nothing</span>
                                    }
                                    else
                                    {
                                        foreach (SetupCheckRowView row in noted)
                                        {
                                            <span class="pill warn">@row.Name failed, recorded but not required</span>
                                        }
                                    }
                                </td>
                            </tr>
                        }
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            }
        </section>
    }

    <p class="muted">A name with something noted against it was chosen anyway, because the rule in
       force that evening, generation @e.LatestEveningGeneration, recorded that check without
       requiring it. It is shown because a later rule may require it, and then the same name would
       not be chosen. The full verdict on every name, chosen or not, is on the
       <a href="/setups">Setups</a> screen.</p>
}
